        {
            "title": "FTPGuard",
            "repo": "AmraniCh/ftp-ids-ml",
            "subtitle": "ML-Based Intrusion Detection for FTP Servers",
            "date": "May 2026 – Jun 2026",
            "paragraphs": [
                "A host-based intrusion detection system for FTP servers that combines machine learning with rule-based signatures, evaluated on real production FTP sessions (from the EC2 instance that hosts my portfolio website).",
                "It reads the vsftpd logs and groups them by session. For each session, we extract 17 features about user behavior, and then an Isolation Forest model gives it a score between 0 and 1. For static and known attacks like CVE-2011-2523, brute force and others, we rely on signature rules.",
                "It includes a Flask dashboard (Chart.js + Tailwind CSS) with real-time alert monitoring, session review, and a feedback loop that lets users correct false positives and retrain the model."
            ],
            "stack": [
                "Python",
                "Machine Learning",
                "Isolation Forest",
                "scikit-learn",
                "Jupyter",
                "Flask",
